DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aauuddiittddiissttdd daemon is responsible for distributing audit trail files
     over a TCP/IP network in a secure and reliable way.

     The aauuddiittddiissttdd daemon can be started with the following command line ar‐
     guments:

     --cc _c_o_n_f_i_g   Specify an alternative location of the configuration file.
                 The default location is _/_e_t_c_/_s_e_c_u_r_i_t_y_/_a_u_d_i_t_d_i_s_t_d_._c_o_n_f.  Note:
                 the configuration file may contain passwords.  Care should be
                 taken to configure proper permissions on this file (eg.
                 0600).

     --dd          Print or log debugging information.  This option can be spec‐
                 ified multiple times to raise the verbosity level.

     --FF          Start the aauuddiittddiissttdd daemon in the foreground.  By default
                 aauuddiittddiissttdd starts in the background.

     --hh          Print the aauuddiittddiissttdd usage message.

     --ll          Start in a launchd-friendly mode, ie. do not use daemon(3).

     --PP _p_i_d_f_i_l_e  Specify an alternative location of a file where main process
                 PID will be stored.  The default location is
                 _/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_a_u_d_i_t_d_i_s_t_d_._p_i_d.

